Actually, wait. Let me reconsider whether I can trigger the overflow with a single SOT by making `nb_tps` smaller.

What if the TLM declares 0 tile-parts for tile 0? Then `opj_j2k_build_tp_index_from_tlm` fails (because all tiles must have at least 1 tile-part), and `m_tlm.m_is_invalid` is set to true. Then the SOT handler allocates `tp_index` with `current_nb_tps` elements (initially 10, growing as needed). So no overflow.

What if the TLM declares 1 tile-part for tile 0, but the SOT declares TPsot=0? Then `current_tpsno=0 < nb_tps=1`. No overflow.

Hmm. So I really need 2 SOT markers.

